Another nice alternative is a public server such as nethack.alt.org.  I
play on this server pretty much exclusively now in spite of having a
perfectly good nethack program on my home machine.  I find it more fun for
various reasons, such as

- bones files
- a high score list that has *other players* on it!
- various game statistics are accessible (http://alt.org/nethack)
- you can watch other people's games as they play them
- if you join #nethack on freenode (irc), a bot announces YASDs and
  ascensions on the channel.  Many other people who play on the server
  also chat on this channel.


